  "worked_solution": "The correct answer is the following.\n\n  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981048/assets/c6cfdc41036d1dc319054c0cf397276f40faa2c749ea59820b45875cb31b3d9f.png)\n\n    \n\nIndeed, we have that $h(x)$ is continuous on the open interval $(-2,\\infty ).$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=0,$ but this point lies within the interval $(-2,\\infty ),$\n\n- $q(x)$ and $p(x)$ are not continuous at $x=1,$ but this point lies within the interval $(-2,\\infty ),$\n\n- $g(x)$is not continuous at $x=2,$ but this point lies within the interval $(-2,\\infty ).$",
